      "purpose": "Defines Flow types for Suspense/SuspenseList internal state and a helper to locate the first suspended fiber in a row or subtree during React reconciliation.",
      "summary": "This file is part of React's reconciler. It exports Flow type definitions describing the internal state of a Suspense boundary (SuspenseState), the rendering state of a SuspenseList (SuspenseListRenderState), and a retry queue (RetryQueue). It also provides findFirstSuspended, a synchronous tree-traversal utility that walks a fiber row (and its children) to find the first fiber that is currently suspended — either a Suspense boundary whose dehydrated state is null/pending/fallback, or a SuspenseList that captured a suspense event (excluding independent reveal order). The traversal mutates return pointers on child and sibling fibers temporarily but performs no allocation or I/O.",
